    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 235\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 6012, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the social services law, in relation to school-\n      based health centers\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would amend the Social Services Law  to  permanently  exempt\nservices  provided  by  school-based  health  centers  (SBHCs)  from the\nrequirement that they be delivered through a Medicaid managed care plan.\n \n  I fully support the  role  that  SBHCs  play  in  providing  important\nmedical,  dental,  and  behavioral  health  care  to  children and young\nadults.  However, as drafted, this bill sets a precedent that is contra-\nry to the State Medicaid  Redesign  Team  recommendation  that  Medicaid\npopulations  be  transitioned  to managed care so that all their medical\nservice needs may be better coordinated, resulting in  improved  service\nquality at an efficient cost.\n \n  While I am constrained to veto this bill for this reason, I appreciate\nthat SBHCs need more time to implement the care coordination and quality\nimprovement  activities required to transition to managed care. As such,\nI am directing the Department of Health to delay inclusion of  SBHCs  in\nmanaged  care until January 1, 2021. During this time, the Department is\ndirected to continue to engage with SBHCs, SBHC  sponsoring  facilities,\nincluding  hospitals and community centers, Performing Provider Systems,\nand managed care companies  to  implement  provider  and  administrative\nagreements  that  facilitate  the  sharing of SBHC patient level data to\nimprove quality, outcomes, and care  coordination  consistent  with  the\nDelivery System Reform Incentive Payment Program goals and projects.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
